From 6ed3d12b184a27d21c0fa41d43269ff6bd17f1e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naster17 <naster17.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:41:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Implement native gfx1013 structured sparse first-order
 backward

Raw compression/matmul lacked derivatives. Public sparse backward also needed a
transpose pack that is not generally a valid row-sparse matrix, and conversion
severed the source dense weight's gradient edge. Add retained-slot GPU backward
formulas, a dense GPU transpose fallback and lazy differentiable conversion.
Handle absent saved optional tensors as undefined as well as nullopt.

Enable source-only spin lint without standalone codegen using an opt-in environment
flag, and apply the configured formatting checks to A04/A05 code. Existing default
lint behavior is unchanged. Convolution/loss and A04 test formatting preserve ASTs.

Test Plan:
```text
python -m pip install -e . -v --no-build-isolation
python test_bc250_sparse_autograd.py -v
PYTORCH_LINT_SKIP_CODEGEN=1 spin lint -- --take=PYFMT,RUFF,FLAKE8,CLANGFORMAT,NEWLINE,INCLUDE,NATIVEFUNCTIONS,TESTOWNERS,TEST_HAS_MAIN,IMPORT_LINTER,SET_LINTER,DOCSTRING_LINTER <affected-files>
lintrunner -a --take=PYFMT,RUFF,FLAKE8,CLANGFORMAT,NEWLINE,INCLUDE,NATIVEFUNCTIONS,TESTOWNERS,TEST_HAS_MAIN,IMPORT_LINTER,SET_LINTER,DOCSTRING_LINTER <affected-files>
```
Separate candidate on native BC-250:38 GPU backward tests pass CPU references,
including all gradients, retained zero slots and independent gradient subsets;
20 A04 forward cases/120 matmuls and seven core groups pass. Guards acknowledged,
dmesg unchanged. First import-order/undefined-optional failures and failed builds
are retained. Targeted lint checks now pass after verified tool initialization.
No integer/higher-order/compile/graph or universal sparse speedup claim. Dense
GPU backward intermediates intentionally prioritize correctness.

Authored with an AI assistant.
